    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0283" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg171"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/2513</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I approve of the course
                    proposed in this letter. I take it for granted that everything necessary would
                    be done to protect the Chinese Government against such unconscionable
                    arrangements as were contemplated by the former consortium, because I am afraid
                    it is not less but rather more likely that the Chinese Government would permit
                    unfair advantage to be taken of it at the present time of stress than
                    formerly.</p>
                <p>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
